UPDATE companies SET description='Selhorst Woodworks operates from Las Vegas, Nevada, where husband-and-wife founders Matthew and Chantel Selhorst established the family-owned business on a shared vision to create exceptional spaces through thoughtful design and expert craftsmanship. What began as a passion for woodworking has grown into a custom finish carpentry company serving the Las Vegas area from its facility on East Patrick Lane.

The shop specializes in custom-milled architectural woodwork including accent walls, accent ceilings, barn doors, shelving, built-ins, mudrooms, baseboards, crown molding, and structural beams. The team also works with specialty materials such as Thermory thermally modified wood and Renson products, and provides design services and wallpaper installation. Projects range from single-room focal points to whole-home millwork packages.

Clients include homeowners, interior designers, builders, and architects who value timeless design and meticulous attention to detail. The company collaborates directly with design professionals and general contractors on residential new-build and renovation projects throughout the Las Vegas market.

The Selhorsts emphasize a family-first approach, treating each project with the same care they would apply in their own home. They position the business on a seamless client experience from initial consultation through final installation, with a focus on the smallest details that make the biggest impact and craftsmanship intended to stand the test of time.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Accent wall fabrication and installation", "Accent ceiling fabrication and installation", "Barn door fabrication and installation", "Custom shelving", "Built-in cabinetry", "Mudroom construction", "Baseboard installation", "Crown molding installation", "Custom beam fabrication", "Thermory wood installation", "Renson product installation", "Design services", "Wallpaper installation"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Interior design", "Architecture", "Custom home building", "Home renovation"], "materials": ["Wood", "Thermory thermally modified wood", "Renson products", "Paint"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated by founders Matthew and Chantel Selhorst", "Specialty in custom finish carpentry and architectural millwork", "Works with Thermory and Renson specialty wood products", "Serves homeowners, interior designers, builders, and architects", "End-to-end service from design consultation through installation"], "facts_used": ["Location: Las Vegas, NV -> db", "Founders: Matthew and Chantel Selhorst -> /", "Ownership: Family-owned -> /", "Services: Accent walls, ceilings, barn doors, shelving, built-ins, mudrooms, baseboards, crown molding, beams -> /services", "Specialty materials: Thermory, Renson -> /services", "Industries served: Homeowners, interior designers, builders, architects -> /", "Address: 3855 East Patrick Lane -> /", "Design services and wallpaper -> /", "Instagram presence mentioned -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "one of Las Vegas'' premier custom finish carpentry companies", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='selhorst-woodworks-las-vegas-san-diego-accent-walls-and-ceilings-barn-doors-shelving-beams' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sentinel Solar operates from Covington, Kentucky, serving customers across Kentucky and Ohio. The company was founded by Jan Thurman, a solar veteran with over a decade of coast-to-coast experience in residential and commercial system design and installation. Thurman launched the business on a simple conviction: solar should be done right, or not at all, emphasizing precision engineering and long-term craftsmanship over volume.

The firm provides full-service solar and storage solutions, handling every step from initial consultation and custom system design through permitting, utility approval, and professional installation. Each project is tailored to the specific roof, energy usage, and goals of the customer, with ongoing production monitoring and long-term support.

Sentinel Solar works with both homeowners and businesses. Recent installations include a system for Heatherbrook Farms in Fort Mitchell, Kentucky, and a commercial array for Wenzel Distillery in Cincinnati, Ohio. The company also serves residential clients in neighborhoods such as Indian Hill, demonstrating experience across agricultural, industrial, and high-end residential sectors.

Thurman positions the company as a premium alternative to high-volume installers, citing four pillars: a consultative, no-pressure sales process; local accountability as an independent, non-franchise operation; installer-first design that prioritizes crew safety and build quality; and a referral-driven model that ties long-term relationships to sustained performance. The company is licensed and insured in both Kentucky and Ohio.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom solar system design", "Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Battery storage integration", "EV charger installation", "Backup generator installation", "Full-service permitting", "Utility interconnection approval", "Production monitoring", "Ongoing maintenance and support"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Consultative, no-pressure sales approach", "Local ownership and accountability (non-franchise)", "Installer-first design for crew safety and build quality", "Referral-driven long-term relationships"], "facts_used": ["Location: Covington, Kentucky -> db", "Founder: Jan Thurman -> /about", "Founding conviction: solar should be done right -> /about", "Services: residential and commercial solar + storage, EV charger, generator -> /, /about", "Projects: Heatherbrook Farms (Fort Mitchell, KY), Wenzel Distillery (Cincinnati, OH), Indian Hill (Cincinnati, OH) -> /", "Licensed & insured in KY & OH -> /", "Values: premium not transactional, local accountability, installer-first quality, long-term relationships -> /about", "Full-service permitting -> db", "Over a decade of coast-to-coast experience -> /about", "Company not a volume shop -> /about", "Referral-driven leads -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Expert design, professional installation, and lasting energy savings \u2014 from a local team with over a decade of coast-to-coast experience.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sentinel-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Servall Uniform & Linen Supply was founded in 1938 in Rapid City, South Dakota. The company began by serving its hometown and gradually expanded across a two-state region, establishing additional locations in Chamberlain, South Dakota, and Gillette, Wyoming.

The business provides uniform rental and direct purchase, linen rental and laundry, janitorial supplies, dust control products, restroom services, first aid supplies, floor mats, towel and bedding rental, hand sanitizer, and ice melt. It operates across western South Dakota and eastern Wyoming, serving hundreds of businesses from its regional facilities.

Customers include healthcare providers such as Spearfish Canyon Healthcare, financial institutions like First Interstate Bank, hospitality and retail operations including Wall Drug and Alternative Fuel Coffee House, and publishing firms such as Ravellette Publications. The company focuses on businesses that require regular uniform and linen programs alongside facility maintenance supplies.

Servall emphasizes dependable, locally supported service, stating that the cost value and convenience of its rental programs become evident within weeks. The company positions itself as a partner that helps businesses maintain professional appearance and workplace safety through scheduled deliveries and responsive account management.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Uniform rental", "Direct uniform purchase", "Linen rental", "Linen laundry service", "Janitorial supply", "Dust control products", "Restroom service", "First aid supply", "Floor mat rental", "Towel and bedding rental", "Hand sanitizer supply", "Ice melt supply"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Regional service across South Dakota and Wyoming since 1938", "Physical locations in Rapid City, Chamberlain, and Gillette for local support", "Integrated uniform, linen, and facility supply programs", "Scheduled laundry and rental services with regular delivery", "Restroom, first aid, and floor care supply programs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1938 -> db", "Headquartered in Rapid City, SD -> db", "Physical locations in Chamberlain, SD and Gillette, WY -> /", "Services South Dakota and Wyoming -> /", "Offers uniform rentals, linen rentals, first aid supplies, janitorial supplies, restroom services -> /", "Provides laundry services -> /", "Serves businesses like Spearfish Canyon Healthcare, First Interstate Bank -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "dependable linen rentals and uniform services", "founded_year": "1938", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='servall-uniform-linen-supply' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Service Electric Cable TV & Communications is headquartered in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania, where it consolidated operations in 2014. The company traces its origins to 1948, when founder John Walson Sr. (born John Walsonavich) extended a coaxial cable from an antenna atop Broad Mountain to his appliance store in Mahanoy City, creating the first community antenna television system in the United States. Now a third-generation family business, it remains under the leadership of the Walson family, with John M. Walson serving as president since 2012.

The company provides cable television, broadband internet, and telephone services across the Lehigh Valley, Hunterdon County (NJ), and Wilkes-Barre regions. Residential offerings include a low-cost Broadband TV package with hundreds of channels and no hidden fees, plus Gig+ internet speeds paired with eero whole-home WiFi. For commercial customers, Service Electric Business delivers dedicated internet, voice, and cable TV with free local, same-day service calls. The firm also operates the Service Electric Network (SEN), a three-channel local network producing high school and collegiate sports, community events, and festival coverage.

Customers range from individual households to small, medium, and enterprise-level businesses throughout eastern Pennsylvania and western New Jersey. Partnerships with PenTeleData and Alianza extend internet and voice capabilities, while membership in the America''s Communications Association and the Broadband Communications Association of Pennsylvania underscores industry engagement.

Service Electric emphasizes its deep community roots and pioneering history—it was the first U.S. cable system to offer Home Box Office in 1972 and among the earliest to deploy two-way cable modems. The company cites its family ownership, local workforce, and commitment to same-day business support as key differentiators in a market dominated by national providers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable television distribution", "Broadband internet service (up to Gig+ speeds)", "Voice over IP telephone service", "Business communications (internet, phone, cable TV)", "Local content production and broadcasting (Service Electric Network)", "Whole-home WiFi deployment (eero)", "Two-way cable modem deployment"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "Cable television", "Broadband internet", "Business communications"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Free local, same-day service calls for business customers", "No network fees, cable TV fees, sports channel fees, or rental fees on Broadband TV", "Gig+ internet speeds with eero whole-home WiFi and local support", "Exclusive local content via Service Electric Network (SEN) at no extra charge", "Third-generation family ownership with over 75 years of community presence"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania since 2014 -> /about", "Founded in 1948 by John Walson Sr. -> /about", "Third-generation family ownership, currently led by John M. Walson -> /about", "Provides cable TV, broadband internet, and telephone services in Lehigh Valley, Hunterdon, Wilkes-Barre -> /services", "Offers Broadband TV at $19.95/month with no hidden fees -> /", "Gig+ internet speeds with eero whole-home WiFi -> /services", "Business division offers free local, same-day service calls -> /services", "Operates Service Electric Network (SEN) with three channels of local sports and events -> /", "First U.S. cable system to offer HBO in 1972 -> /about", "Deployed first two-way cable modems in Lehigh Valley in 1999 -> /about", "Partnerships with PenTeleData and Alianza -> /about", "Member of America''s Communications Association and Broadband Communications Association of Pennsylvania -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Service Electric Business is a local leader in business communications services, offering Internet, phone, and cable TV with free local, same-day service calls.", "founded_year": "1948", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='service-electric-cable-tv-communications-bethlehem-hq' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Service Metal Fabricators operates from Williamsburg, Virginia, where it has provided precision sheet metal fabrication for over 40 years. The company does not disclose its founding year or founders, and ownership details are not publicly stated.

The shop specializes in NEMA-rated electronic enclosures, brackets, panels, assemblies, and stainless-steel medical containers. Its process lineup includes shearing, CNC punching, press-brake forming, vertical milling, MIG/TIG and spot welding, hardware insertion, riveting, mechanical assembly, silk-screening, chemical finishing, powder coating, and painting. Work is performed in a 12-acre, 56,000-square-foot facility (also described as 60,000 square feet) with machine redundancy to support scaling. Headcount is not published, though the quality department maintains a ratio of three QA professionals for every 25 production staff.

Customers span electronics, industrial equipment, diagnostic and measurement devices, medical, aerospace, defense, transportation, solar energy, and TEMPEST computing. Named references include Becton Dickinson’s laboratory blood-analyzer systems, a $15 billion transportation company’s electronics division, an emerging smart-circuitry solar firm, helm stations for a dozen U.S. aircraft carriers, and various components for U.S. armed forces machinery.

The company differentiates itself through vertical integration—operating its own delivery fleet and offering free shipping within 200 miles—in-house design engineering and DFM support, reverse-engineering capability, and a quality program that adheres to ISO guidelines, MIL-DTL-5541, AMS-STD-1595, RoHS, and numerous other military and federal standards.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO compliant','MIL-DTL-5541','AMS-STD-1595','RoHS Compliant','FED-STD-595','MS51835','NASM8846D']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Shearing", "CNC Punching", "Press Brake Forming", "CNC Forming", "Vertical Milling", "CNC Machining", "MIG/TIG Welding", "Spot Welding", "Hardware Installation", "Riveting", "Mechanical Assembly", "Silk Screening", "Part Marking", "Chemical Finishing", "Powder Coating", "Painting", "Plating", "Phoscoat Steel", "Chromate Conversion Coating (MIL-DTL-5541)", "Surface Graining & Deburring", "Prototyping", "Design for Manufacturing (DFM)", "Engineering Design Assistance", "Quality Assurance Inspection", "Reverse Engineering"], "industries": ["Electronics", "Industrial Equipment", "Diagnostic & Measurement", "Medical", "Aerospace", "Defense / Military", "Transportation", "Solar Energy", "TEMPEST Computing"], "materials": ["Stainless Steel", "Aluminum", "Steel"], "equipment": ["Strippit CNC Punch Presses (4)", "Haas Precision CNC Vertical Mills (3)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.002\u20130.004 inch (CNC punch presses)", "built_on": ["Own delivery fleet with free shipping within 200 miles", "Machine redundancy for on-time delivery", "ISO-compliant quality system with adherence to military specs (MIL-DTL-5541, AMS-STD-1595)", "Design engineering, DFM, and reverse-engineering support"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Williamsburg, Virginia -> db", "Over 40 years in business -> /", "Facility: 12-acre, 56,000 sq ft -> /", "Facility: 60,000 sq ft -> /about-us", "Specializes in NEMA enclosures, brackets, panels, assemblies, stainless steel medical containers -> /", "Processes: shearing, CNC punching, surface finishing, vertical milling, hardware installation, MIG/TIG welding, press brake forming, spot welding, riveting, mechanical assembly, silk-screening, chemical finishing, paint/powder coating, prototyping, DFM -> /, /services", "Vertical integration: own delivery fleet, free delivery within 200 miles -> /", "Machine redundancy ensures timely delivery -> /about-us", "QA staffing: 3 QA professionals per 25 production staff -> /quality", "Equipment: 4 Strippit CNC Punch Presses, 3 Haas Precision CNC Vertical Mills -> /quality", "Tolerances: .002-.004 inch for punch presses -> /quality", "Certifications: ISO compliant, MIL-DTL-5541, AMS-STD-1595, RoHS, FED-STD-595, MS51835, NASM8846D -> /quality", "Industries served: electronics, industrials, diagnostic/measurement, medical, aerospace, military, transportation, solar, TEMPEST computing -> /about-us", "Customers: Becton Dickinson, $15B transportation company, solar company, US aircraft carriers, US armed forces -> /about-us", "Design engineering and DFM assistance -> /", "Reverse engineering capability -> /", "Materials: stainless steel, aluminum, steel -> /, /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Service Metal Fabricators is a one-stop shop providing comprehensive precision sheet metal fabrication services", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='service-metal-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Seven Trees Woodworking was founded in 2009 by Jarin Smoker in New Holland, Pennsylvania. Smoker''s lifelong passion for fine millwork became the foundation of the business, which has since grown into a team of skilled craftsmen dedicated to transforming raw wood into high-quality architectural pieces for a diverse clientele.

The shop produces custom architectural millwork, including cabinetry, doors, and commercial millwork, as well as private-label and white-label furniture for international brands. In-house capabilities cover CNC machining, drafting, and metalwork, allowing the company to handle projects from design through fabrication under one roof.

The company serves the restaurant and hospitality industries, along with commercial, residential, and office sectors.

