UPDATE companies SET description='Severance Foods, operating under the Pan De Oro brand, has been producing tortilla chips in Hartford, Connecticut since 1985. The company was founded by three food scientists—Richard Stevens, John Grikis, and Rich Dana—who had developed products such as Ortega Mexican Foods for Heublein, Inc. When R.J. Reynolds acquired Heublein in 1984 and planned to relocate operations to California, the trio used their severance packages to establish their own facility in the Northeast, anticipating rising demand for Mexican-style foods in the region.

Today, Severance Foods describes itself as the largest manufacturer and co-packer of tortilla chips in the Northeast. From its plant in Hartford, the company produces its own Pan De Oro line of non‑GMO, organic, hand‑crafted tortilla chips and salsa, while also providing contract manufacturing and co‑packing services for other brands. The operation emphasizes all‑natural ingredients and proprietary flavor development rooted in the founders’ product‑development background.

The company’s customer base spans foodservice, institutional, and retail channels. Pan De Oro products have been supplied to restaurants, schools, and concession stands since 1985, and the brand now appears in grocery stores and farmers markets across New York, New Jersey, and Pennsylvania.

The founders’ original motivation was to fill a regional supply gap for tortilla products, and the company continues to differentiate itself through a family‑owned, hands‑on approach that prioritizes ingredient transparency—non‑GMO, organic, and free of artificial additives—and a hand‑crafted process that the firm says preserves texture and flavor.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Tortilla chip manufacturing", "Salsa manufacturing", "Co-packing / contract manufacturing", "Product development", "Quality assurance"], "industries": ["Foodservice (restaurants)", "Education (schools)", "Concessions / venues", "Retail (grocery, specialty, farmers markets)", "Contract food manufacturing (co-packing)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1985 by Richard Stevens, John Grikis, Rich Dana after Heublein acquisition -> /about", "Family-owned and operated since 1985 -> /, /about", "Largest manufacturer and co-packer of tortilla chips in the Northeast -> /about", "Produces non-GMO, organic, hand-crafted tortilla chips and salsa under Pan De Oro brand -> /, /about", "Supplies restaurants, schools, concessions since 1985; retail in NY, NJ, PA -> /about, /", "Headquarters at 3478 Main Street, Hartford, CT -> /, /about", "LinkedIn URL provided -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, Severance Foods is the largest manufacturer and co-packer of tortilla chips in the northeast.", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/pan-de-oro-tortilla-chip-company/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='severance-foods-pan-de-oro' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Shaker Furniture of Maine operates from a two-floor, nearly 10,000-square-foot showroom on Route 1 in Scarborough, Maine. The business is led by proprietor Steve Celona, who emphasizes American-made craftsmanship.

The company offers solid wood furniture crafted from native hardwoods including cherry, maple, and oak, as well as classic pine pieces. Every piece is solid wood, made in American shops, and available prefinished or ready for paint or stain. The shop also provides custom building to customer specifications. The facility spans two floors and nearly 10,000 square feet, displaying bedrooms, living rooms, dining sets, and accent pieces.

Shaker Furniture of Maine serves residential customers nationwide, shipping furniture across the United States. Its showroom caters to homeowners seeking bedroom, living room, dining, and occasional furniture, with an emphasis on personal service and value-driven pricing.

The company differentiates itself with a "Made in Maine and Made in America" commitment, highlighting solid wood construction, timeless designs, and expert personal service as the foundation of its shopping experience. Celona states the goal is to introduce comfortable, lasting furniture to enhance life at home.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture building", "Solid wood furniture manufacturing", "Prefinishing", "Stain/paint preparation", "Nationwide shipping", "Retail showroom", "Pine furniture", "Dining tables", "Coffee tables", "Dressers", "Beds", "Buffets", "Cabinets", "Chairs", "Chests", "Desks", "End tables", "Entertainment units", "Occasional tables", "Office furniture", "Patio furniture", "Recliners", "Seating", "Furniture sets"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Cherry", "Maple", "Oak", "Pine"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Made in Maine and Made in America", "Solid wood construction", "Custom building to specifications", "Expert personal service", "Value-driven pricing", "Nationwide shipping"], "facts_used": ["Location: Scarborough, Maine -> db", "Address: 715 Route 1, Scarborough, ME -> /", "Proprietor: Steve Celona -> /", "Facility: two floors, nearly 10,000 sq ft -> /", "Materials: cherry, maple, oak, pine -> /", "Products: solid wood furniture, custom building -> /", "Shipping: nationwide -> /", "Differentiators: Made in Maine, solid wood, personal service, value pricing -> /", "Capabilities from db: Pine Furniture, Dining Tables, Coffee Tables, Dressers -> db", "Product categories from page: beds, buffets, cabinets, chairs, chests, desks, end tables, entertainment, occasional tables, office & bookcases, patio & outdoor, recliners, seating, sets, stands, stools -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Every single piece is solid wood, and made with pride in American shops. We''ll even custom-build to your specifications!", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='shaker-furniture-of-maine' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sheet Metal Enterprises operates from Dedham, Massachusetts, on the Boston–Dedham line just off I‑95. The shop is a family‑owned business run by Ed, who brings more than 30 years of HVAC and fabrication experience, including 22 years installing residential and commercial systems in the field. The company has been in operation for over a decade, leveraging that hands‑on background to guide customers through sizing and design decisions.

The shop specializes in custom HVAC ductwork and copper shower pans, along with other made‑to‑order sheet metal products. Ducts are produced in standard 4‑foot and 8‑foot lengths, but the team routinely cuts pieces to exact fractional dimensions — such as 74 3/4 inches — and solders brass strainers into shower pans. A delivery service drops finished orders directly at job sites, and the location near local HVAC supply houses helps keep turnaround times short for a custom fabrication operation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom HVAC ductwork fabrication", "Copper shower pan fabrication", "Custom sheet metal fabrication", "Soldering of brass fittings", "Job-site delivery"], "industries": ["HVAC", "Plumbing", "Construction", "Residential building", "Commercial building"], "materials": ["Sheet metal", "Copper", "Brass"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Owner Ed has 30+ years HVAC and fabrication experience", "Fast turnaround for a custom fabrication shop", "Job\u2011site delivery service", "Custom ductwork cut to fractional-inch dimensions", "Located minutes from HVAC supply houses"], "facts_used": ["Location: Dedham, MA on Boston/Dedham line near I-95 -> homepage", "Family owned/operated -> homepage", "Owner Ed with 30+ years HVAC/fabrication experience, 22 years field installation -> /about", "Over 10 years in business -> /about", "Custom HVAC ductwork fabrication, 4ft/8ft lengths, custom sizes -> homepage", "Copper shower pans with soldered brass strainers -> homepage", "Delivery service to job sites -> homepage", "Fast turnaround for custom fabrication shop -> /about", "Located near HVAC supply houses -> /about", "Serves HVAC contractors, plumbers, residential/commercial -> inferred from /about and homepage"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a custom fabrication shop that specializes in hvac duct work and copper pans.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sheet-metal-enterprises' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sherven Sales, Inc., based in Wahpeton, North Dakota, has been family-owned and operated since its founding in 1970. The company began as a supplier of agricultural equipment and has remained under family stewardship for over five decades.

The business supplies and assembles a range of farm equipment, including grain bins and handling systems, livestock handling equipment, and flatbed, enclosed, and stock trailers. It provides full assembly and ongoing service for every product it sells, operating as a full-service dealer for agricultural operations.

Sherven Sales serves grain farmers, livestock producers, and commercial grain-handling facilities across the region. Its customer base includes family farms and larger agricultural enterprises that rely on the company for equipment procurement, installation, and maintenance.

The company distinguishes itself through its long-standing family ownership and its commitment to assembling and servicing all equipment it sells, offering a single point of contact for agricultural equipment needs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Equipment assembly", "Equipment service and maintenance", "Grain handling system installation", "Livestock equipment installation", "Trailer service"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Grain handling", "Livestock farming"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Grain bins", "Grain handling equipment", "Livestock equipment", "Flatbed trailers", "Enclosed trailers", "Stock trailers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1970", "Full assembly and service on all equipment sold", "Specialized in grain systems, livestock equipment, and trailers"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1970 -> db", "Family-owned and operated -> /about", "Headquarters in Wahpeton, North Dakota -> /", "Specializes in grain systems, grain handling equipment, livestock equipment, and trailers -> /about", "Offers assembly and service of all products sold -> /about", "Product categories: Grain Bins & Handling Equipment, Livestock Equipment, Flatbed, Enclosed & Stock Trailers -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We specialize in grain systems, grain handling equipment, livestock equipment, and trailers. We offer assembly and service of all the products we sell.", "founded_year": "1970", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sherven-s-grain-livestock' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SiCamore Semi operates a pure-play semiconductor foundry in Bend, Oregon, drawing on more than 30 years of wafer-fabrication experience. The company focuses on wide-bandgap materials such as silicon carbide (SiC) and gallium nitride (GaN) to serve high-voltage, high-power applications.

The foundry runs 100 mm and 150 mm production lines for silicon and SiC, offering single-step device manufacturing, multi-project wafer (MPW) service, and a dedicated gold fab for high-reliability, radiation-hardened, and RF devices. Process capabilities include photolithography with ASML 5000 I-line steppers and Karl Suss aligners, thin-film deposition (sputtering, PVD, CVD, PECVD, e-beam evaporation), frontside/backside metal stacks, thermal oxidation and diffusion, wet and plasma dry etching, RIE, rapid thermal annealing, and cold/hot ion implantation. SiC-specific steps cover high-temperature implant/anneal and gate oxidation with nitric oxide anneal. Partner services extend to device design, wafer thinning, dicing, packaging, and test.

Customers span electric-vehicle drivetrain suppliers, medical-device makers (monitoring, diagnostic, therapeutic), industrial OEMs in agriculture, data centers, energy, and robotics, aerospace and defense programs requiring ITAR-compliant fabrication, and academic partners collaborating on NASA, NSF, DOE, and DOD grants. The company supplies SiC diodes, MOSFETs, JBSFETs, JFETs, IGBTs, Si SGTOs, and SDIODEs to these markets.

SiCamore Semi states its mission is to deliver innovative power-semiconductor solutions through silicon, SiC, GaN, and photonics technologies, aiming to become the wide-bandgap fabrication facility in the U.S. Northwest for both government agencies and commercial sectors such as transportation, telecommunications, and healthcare infrastructure.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["100mm & 150mm wafer production for Si and SiC", "Photolithography (ASML5000 I-Line Steppers, Karl Suss Aligners)", "Thin film deposition (sputtering, PVD, CVD, PECVD, E-beam evaporation)", "Frontside/backside metal deposition (Ti/TiW/AlCu, Ti/Ni/Ag, Ti/Pt/Au, AlSiCu)", "Thermal oxidation and diffusion (Thermco, MRL)", "Wet chemical etch", "Plasma dry etch", "RIE etch", "Rapid thermal annealing (RTA)", "Ion implantation (cold and hot)", "SiC single-step process", "High-temperature implant and annealing", "Gate oxidation with nitric oxide anneal", "Gold wafer fab for HiRel/Rad Hard/RF", "Multi-project wafer (MPW) service", "Wafer probe with Keysight B1505A", "Device design", "Wafer thinning", "Wafer dicing", "Packaging and test"], "industries": ["Electric Vehicles", "Medical", "Industrial", "Aerospace & Defense", "Academia", "Transportation", "Telecommunications", "Healthcare Infrastructure"], "materials": ["Silicon", "Silicon Carbide (SiC)", "Gallium Nitride (GaN)", "Gold"], "equipment": ["ASML5000 I-Line Steppers", "Karl Suss Aligners", "Thermco", "MRL", "Keysight B1505A power device analyzer/curve tracer"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Pure-play foundry for advanced wide-bandgap power semiconductors", "ITAR-certified secure fabrication environment", "100 mm and 150 mm wafer lines for silicon and SiC with single-step device manufacturing", "Dedicated gold wafer fab for HiRel, radiation-hardened, and RF devices", "Multi-project wafer (MPW) service and quick single-process-step turns"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bend, Oregon ->