UPDATE companies SET description='Simplex Fabrication operates from Woodbine, Maryland, where owner Seth Neilson began the business roughly a decade ago after teaching himself to weld with an inexpensive TIG welder. The venture started as a garage hobby repairing an old Nissan and grew into a full-time fabrication shop. Neilson remains the sole proprietor and primary welder-fabricator.

The shop provides welding, CNC plasma cutting, and general metal fabrication services. Work ranges from rust repair on automotive and equipment parts to one-off custom builds such as a go-kart belt sander and a climbing-saddle hunting tree stand. Neilson handles quoting, fabrication, and finishing himself, keeping the operation lean and flexible.

Customers include hobbyists, equipment owners needing repairs, and individuals with custom project ideas. The shop does not target a specific industry but serves anyone requiring metal fabrication or welding, from small repairs to prototype-level assemblies.

Neilson says the business was born from a passion for welding and a drive to innovate better ways of building things. That mindset shapes the shop''s approach: taking a customer''s concept and turning it into a finished metal piece, whether it''s a cracked lawnmower deck or a novel mechanical design.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Welding (TIG)", "CNC plasma cutting", "Metal fabrication", "Rust repair", "Custom fabrication"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["TIG welder", "CNC plasma cutter"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Concept-to-completion custom fabrication", "Repair and restoration welding (e.g., rust repair)", "CNC plasma cutting for precise profiles", "Owner-operated, direct communication with the fabricator", "Innovation-focused approach to problem-solving"], "facts_used": ["Owner: Seth Neilson -> db", "Location: Woodbine, Maryland -> db", "Started ~10 years ago as hobby with cheap TIG welder -> pages:/", "Services: welding, CNC plasma cutting, fabrication -> db, pages:/", "Projects: rust repair, go-kart belt sander, climbing saddle hunting tree stand -> pages:/", "Business model: custom fabrication and repair for individuals -> pages:/", "Owner-operated, direct quoting via call/text/email -> pages:/"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "I am the owner and welder/fabricator at Simplex Fabrication. If you have an idea you would like to see brought to life, or you just need some cracks rewelded on your lawnmower, I am your guy.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='simplex-fabrication-welding-and-cnc-plasma-cutting' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 2015 in Raleigh, North Carolina, SinnovaTek was established on principles of integrity, creativity, and sustainability. The company became a certified B Corporation in 2017, formalizing a mission to promote worldwide health and wellness by fostering the delivery of high-quality, healthy foods through sustainable methods.

SinnovaTek develops and integrates advanced food processing technologies, manufacturing equipment such as thermal processing systems and pumps, while also offering a suite of integration tools. The company operates a precision-scale aseptic copacking facility for rapid prototyping and product launches, and runs a working pilot plant. Its Vitero™ protein‑polyphenol ingredient technology supports product development and piloting services, and the firm provides R&D and engineering support for food‑industry clients.

The company serves the food processing and food technology sectors, working with both established manufacturers and early‑stage ventures. As a member of the Upcycled Food Association since 2020, SinnovaTek also focuses on upcycling excess food through innovative processing infrastructure.

SinnovaTek differentiates itself by making advanced thermal processing and aseptic systems accessible to companies of all sizes, emphasizing that processed foods can retain high nutritional quality. The certified B Corp status and a team of food scientists and engineers with decades of commercialization experience underpin its approach.', certifications=ARRAY['Certified B Corporation']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Advanced food processing technology development and manufacturing", "R&D and engineering services", "Protein\u2011polyphenol ingredient technology development", "Product development and piloting services", "Precision\u2011scale aseptic food copacking", "Rapid prototyping", "Pilot facility operations", "Equipment manufacturing: advanced thermal processing systems", "Equipment manufacturing: pumps", "Integration and implementation tools", "Food safety processing and validation", "Aseptic food processing", "Advanced thermal processing", "Upcycling food processing infrastructure", "Co\u2011manufacturing (small\u2011scale manufacturing)", "Product commercialization support"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Food technology", "Upcycled food"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Advanced thermal processing systems", "Pumps", "Integration and implementation tools"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified B Corporation since 2017", "Member of Upcycled Food Association since 2020", "End\u2011to\u2011end provider: equipment, ingredient technology, and co\u2011manufacturing", "Precision\u2011scale aseptic copacking for rapid prototyping", "Vitero\u2122 protein\u2011polyphenol ingredient technology"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2015 -> /about-us", "Certified B Corporation in 2017 -> /about-us", "Member of Upcycled Food Association as of 2020 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Raleigh, North Carolina -> db", "Builds and sells advanced thermal processing systems and pumps -> /", "Offers Vitero protein\u2011polyphenol ingredient technology -> /", "Provides precision\u2011scale aseptic food copacking and pilot facility -> /about-us", "Team of food scientists and engineers with decades of experience -> /about-us", "Focus on aseptic food processing and advanced thermal processing -> /about-us", "End\u2011to\u2011end solutions provider for food industry -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "While we build and sell equipment, we also offer a range of tools to make its integration a easier.", "founded_year": "2015", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/sinnovatek-inc./"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sinnovatek' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Siri Wire Co. operates from Danielson, Connecticut, where it was founded in 1992. The company is a fourth‑generation family business, led by the same family that built it from the ground up, with over 50 years of combined industry experience.

The company manufactures and stocks stainless steel and alloy wire, offering grades such as 302, 304, 316, 17‑7, 302HQ, 303, 316L, 410, 416, 420, and 430. Siri Wire maintains one of the largest domestic stocking positions for electro‑polish‑quality (EPQ) wire in the region, enabling same‑day shipping on many sizes. Through its affiliation with the Tri Star Metals family and the Bender Wire Group, the company draws on two fully operational U.S. production mills, providing domestic melt, DFARS‑compliant, and non‑DFARS material options.

Siri Wire serves medical and surgical device makers, filter‑screen and washer producers, automotive suppliers, aerospace and defense contractors, fastener and cold‑heading shops, and general industrial customers. Typical applications include springs, fasteners, medical equipment, filter screens, washers, and rings.

