 "After-sales support from installer -> /", "Tax incentive optimization for commercial -> /services", "Time-of-use optimization and peak shaving -> /services", "Customer examples: rental property owner, Hunter Homes, Piedmont off-grid shop -> /, /services"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Solar Pro provides a complete solution, from initial consultation to installation and monitoring.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solar-pro' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Solar Scapes operates from Grain Valley, Missouri, serving the greater Kansas City metropolitan area. The company was founded by Cory B., who serves as owner and field operator, on the conviction that solar customers deserve ongoing support long after installation. The business began with specialized solar care and maintenance before expanding into a full-service energy partner.

Today Solar Scapes designs and installs solar arrays, provides service and troubleshooting for systems from any manufacturer, and offers the Solar Shield maintenance membership with tiered annual plans that include cleaning, inspections, active monitoring, and thermal imaging. The team also installs FranklinWH and Enphase battery storage, Generac standby generators, and EV charging equipment, and performs solar removal and reinstallation for roof replacements. A crew of three field technicians handles projects across both sides of the state line.

The company serves residential and commercial customers throughout the Kansas City metro, including Overland Park, Olathe, Lenexa, Shawnee, Leawood, Lee’s Summit, Independence, Blue Springs, and Liberty. Clients range from homeowners with orphaned systems whose original installer has disappeared to businesses seeking backup power and electrical upgrades.

Solar Scapes differentiates itself by focusing on long-term system health rather than one-time sales. Its NABCEP-certified technicians service orphaned systems, and the company holds certified installer status for FranklinWH, Enphase, and Generac equipment. The Solar Shield program adds scheduled maintenance, priority scheduling, and detailed reporting to protect production over the system’s 25-year design life.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP Certification','FranklinWH Certified Installer','Enphase Certified Installer','Generac Certified Installer']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar installation", "Solar service & troubleshooting", "Solar maintenance (Solar Shield membership)", "Animal guard installation", "Solar removal & reinstallation", "Battery backup installation (FranklinWH, Enphase)", "Standby generator installation (Generac)", "EV charging installation", "Electrical inspections", "Thermal imaging inspection", "Drone inspection", "Active monitoring & production verification"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Backup power", "Electrical services", "EV charging infrastructure"], "materials": ["Solar panels", "FranklinWH battery storage", "Enphase battery storage", "Generac generators", "EV chargers", "Animal guard materials", "Electrical components"], "equipment": ["Thermal imaging camera", "Drone"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["NABCEP Certified technicians", "Services orphaned solar systems from any manufacturer", "Certified FranklinWH, Enphase, and Generac installer", "Solar Shield maintenance membership with tiered plans", "Active monitoring and thermal imaging diagnostics"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Grain Valley, Missouri -> db", "Founder/owner: Cory B. (Owner & Field Operator) -> /about", "Team members: Grant H. (Field Operations Lead), Eric R. (Field Technician) -> /about", "Services: solar installation, service, maintenance, animal guard, removal/reinstallation, battery backup, gener