UPDATE companies SET description='SparkFun Electronics was founded in 2003 in Niwot, Colorado. The company began with a mission to make electronics accessible to engineers, hobbyists, and educators through open-source components, tutorials, and documentation.

The company designs and manufactures a wide range of open-source hardware, including sensors, microcontroller development boards, and kits, while also distributing third-party components from brands such as Raspberry Pi, Teensy, and NVIDIA. A dedicated subsidiary, SparkPNT, focuses on high-precision positioning, navigation, and timing products built to be durable, future-proof, and repairable. SparkFun operates with approximately 140 employees and offers a custom kit assembly service for educational workshops and classroom curricula.

SparkFun serves engineers, prototypers, hobbyists, product developers, and educators across industries such as education, robotics, Internet of Things (IoT), environmental monitoring, positioning/navigation/timing (PNT), and artificial intelligence/machine learning. Concrete examples from its partner network include AI robots running on NVIDIA Jetson modules, high-precision GPS boards using u-blox technology, DIY heart-rate monitors, and community hackathons.

The company emphasizes open-source hardware and accessible documentation to lower barriers to emerging technology. Its products are designed to be durable, future-proof, and repairable, and it provides a solderless Qwiic modular ecosystem to simplify prototyping. SparkFun also offers volume pricing, a distributor/reseller program, and free domestic shipping on most orders over $100.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Open-source hardware design", "Custom kit assembly", "Volume pricing", "Distributor/reseller program", "Qwiic modular ecosystem", "High-precision PNT product development", "Sensor manufacturing", "Microcontroller board manufacturing", "Educational workshop support"], "industries": ["Education", "Robotics", "Internet of Things (IoT)", "Environmental Monitoring", "Positioning/Navigation/Timing (PNT)", "Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning", "Prototyping", "Hobbyist Electronics", "Product Development"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Open-source hardware design and documentation", "Custom kit assembly service for education and workshops", "Volume pricing and distributor/reseller program", "SparkPNT subsidiary for high-precision PNT products", "Qwiic solderless modular ecosystem"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2003 -> db", "Headquartered in Niwot, Colorado -> db", "140 employees -> db", "Open-source electronics components and tutorials -> /", "Subsidiary SparkPNT for high-precision PNT products -> /", "Custom kit service for education and workshops -> /", "Volume pricing and distributor/reseller program -> /services", "Partners include NVIDIA, u-blox -> /services", "Qwiic modular ecosystem -> /", "Free domestic shipping on orders over $100 -> /", "Products designed to be durable, future-proof, and repairable -> /", "Serves engineers, prototypers, hobbyists, product developers, educators -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type