UPDATE companies SET description='Standex Electronics operates from its headquarters in Fairfield, Ohio, as a global platform company that unifies three specialized divisions: Standex Detect, Standex Edge, and Standex Grid. The business traces its roots through generations of innovation in electronic components, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed. Over time, strategic acquisitions — including Amran and Narayan Powertech, which now anchor the Grid division — have expanded its portfolio into a diversified, vertically integrated operation.

The company designs and manufactures precision-engineered electronic components spanning switching and sensing technologies, power magnetics, and grid solutions. Its product range includes reed switches, relays, sensors, custom transformers, planar transformers, inductors, chokes, EMI components, and low- to medium-voltage instrument transformers. Manufacturing facilities, design centers, and sales offices are distributed across North America, Europe, and Asia, providing local support backed by global resources.

Standex serves mission-critical markets including automotive (passenger, commercial, off-road, construction, and agriculture), aerospace and defense, medical, industrial automation, telecommunications, renewable and alternative energy, and electrical utilities. Customers range from OEMs developing smart-home and transportation systems to utilities modernizing grid infrastructure. The company positions its three divisions to address distinct but complementary needs: Detect for switching and sensing, Edge for magnetics in power conversion, and Grid for instrument transformers and high-voltage components.

Standex says its differentiation lies in the combination of a global footprint with local engineering intimacy, a legacy of innovation across reed switches, magnetics, and power-grid technologies, and a unified operating philosophy — Innovate, Consult, Engineer, Deliver — that guides every program from concept through production.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom engineering solutions", "Design and manufacture of precision electronic components", "Switching and sensing technologies", "Relay design and manufacturing", "Power magnetics (transformers, inductors, planar transformers, chokes, EMI components)", "Instrument transformer design and manufacturing (low and medium voltage)", "High-voltage component manufacturing", "Rapid prototyping", "Vertical integration"], "industries": ["Military and Aerospace", "Renewable Energy", "Telecommunications", "Alternative Energy", "Automotive (Passenger)", "Automotive (Commercial, Off Road, Construction, Agriculture)", "Medical", "Industrial", "Energy/Grid/Utilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Deep vertical integration for consistent quality and rapid prototyping", "Global footprint with local expertise across North America, Europe, and Asia", "Three complementary divisions: Detect (switching/sensing), Edge (magnetics), Grid (instrument transformers)", "Legacy brands Amran and Narayan Powertech integrated into Standex Grid"], "facts_used": ["HQ in Fairfield, Ohio -> db", "Three divisions: Standex Detect, Standex Edge, Standex Grid -> /about", "Products include reed switches, relays, sensors, transformers, inductors, planar transformers, chokes, EMI components, instrument transformers, high-voltage components -> /about, /", "Industries served: Military/Aerospace, Renewable Energy, Telecommunications, Alternative Energy, Automotive, Medical, Industrial, Energy/Grid -> industries_served db, /about", "Global presence across North America, Europe, Asia -> /about", "Acquired Amran and Narayan Powertech for Standex Grid -> /about", "Custom engineering capability -> /capabilities, /about", "Vertical integration for consistent quality and rapid prototyping -> /about", "Engineer-to-engineer collaborative approach -> /capabilities", "Design and manufacture of precision-engineered electronic components -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Standex Electronics is a global leader in the design and manufacture of precision-engineered electronic components.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='standex-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='State Fabricators Inc., known as StateFab, has operated from Farmington Hills, Michigan since its founding in 1946. The company began in a 1,900‑square‑foot space and grew into a production welding shop that now occupies 26,000 square feet under crane on a seven‑acre site with room to stage large jobs.

The shop focuses on custom steel fabrication and production welding, delivering everything from single prototypes to thousand‑unit runs. Its core processes include fixture‑based welding, custom assembly, and large‑scale steel fabrication.

StateFab serves the automotive industry as a long‑time Tier One and Tier Two supplier. Its product portfolio centers on conveyor‑system components: overhead, inverted, skillet, ELPO, paint, door, and cab carriers, as well as line platforms and robot gantries built for tight installation windows. The company also produces skillet frames and custom assemblies for plants across North America.

The company emphasizes repeatability and quality control. A quality manual has been in use since 1997, and certified welders work with dedicated checking fixtures so that each subassembly meets the same standard whether the run is one unit or a thousand. Flexible systems allow the shop to move between large production jobs and small prototype fabrications without changing its workflow.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Production welding", "Custom assembly", "Automotive carrier fabrication (overhead, inverted, skillet, ELPO, paint, door, cab)", "Large steel fabrication (line platforms, robot gantries)", "Fixture design and build", "Checking fixture inspection", "Skillet frame fabrication", "Door and part carrier fabrication", "Custom steel fabrication"], "industries": ["Automotive"], "materials": ["Steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quality manual in continuous use since 1997", "Certified welders on staff", "Checking fixtures for repeatable subassembly verification", "Flexible scheduling for prototype through production volumes", "26,000 sq ft under crane with 7 acres for staging"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1946 -> /", "Headquarters Farmington Hills, Michigan -> /", "26,000 sq ft under crane -> /", "7 acres for staging -> /", "50+ employees (fixture builders, welders, operators) -> /", "Started in 1,900 sq ft -> /", "Quality manual in use since 1997 -> /", "Certified welders -> /", "Checking fixtures for repeatability -> /", "Automotive Tier One and Tier Two supplier -> db (industries_served)", "Products: carriers, skillets, line platforms, robot gantries -> /", "Volume: prototype to thousand-unit run -> /", "Flexible systems for large and small jobs -> db (description)", "Custom steel fabrication focus -> db (description)"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Production weldments for automotive conveyor systems, from one proto