UPDATE companies SET description='Stone Enterprises Inc., based in Omaha, Nebraska, traces its roots to February 2000 when it acquired a small machine shop in Hastings, Nebraska, to produce two components for a food-processing distributor. The company later expanded, purchasing a distributor of replacement parts in 2002 and adding a CNC machine shop to begin custom fabrication. In 2007 it hired its first full-time design engineer, and in 2010 it acquired American Meat Equipment, solidifying its focus on food-processing equipment and parts.

Today the company operates as a precision manufacturer of both custom food-processing equipment and aftermarket replacement parts. Its 35-person team includes three design engineers, nine fabricators, ten master machinists, and twelve support staff. Core capabilities span CNC machining, welding and fabrication, mechanical assembly, and in-house design, with every part individually inspected and tested before shipment. The product line ranges from peelers, vacuum tables, and conveyor systems to custom sinks and stairways, alongside a broad catalog of replacement components for major OEM brands.

Its replacement-parts portfolio covers machines from brands such as Handtmann stuffers, Townsend peelers, Jarvis equipment, KP and CHUB packaging systems, Marel, Multivac, and others.

